<!-- Code System Information -->
<tr>
    <td style="border-bottom: none;"><b>Code System Information</b></td>
    <td>Links</td>
    <td colspan="2"><a href="https://www.eatrightpro.org/practice/nutrition-care-process/ncp-terminology">https://www.eatrightpro.org/practice/nutrition-care-process/ncp-terminology</a></td>
</tr>
 <tr>
    <td style="border-top: none;"><!-- Code System Information --></td>
    <td>Description</td>
    <td colspan="2">
        <div>
        <p>NCPT is a standardized terminology that supports the Nutrition Care Process (NCP), a systematic approach used by registered dietitian nutritionists (RDNs) and nutrition and dietetics technicians, registered (NDTRs) to provide nutrition care. NCPT is organized around the four steps of the NCP; Nutrition Assessment, Nutrition Diagnosis, Nutrition Intervention, and Nutrition Monitoring and Evaluation, and provides standardized terms and a hierarchy to document nutrition care consistently in electronic health records.</p>
        <p>NCPT is maintained by the Academy's NCPT Committee and is mapped to SNOMED CT and LOINC to support interoperable, coded documentation of nutrition care.</p>
        <p>NCPT is published and made accessible to subscribers through the Academy's electronic Nutrition Care Process Terminology (eNCPT) platform at <a href="https://www.ncpro.org/">ncpro.org</a>. eNCPT is the access/delivery platform for NCPT, not a separate terminology.</p>
        </div>
    </td>
 </tr>

